# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0); GitHub renders "Cite this repository" from it.
# No `version` or `date-released`: they would go stale on every release. Cite a
# release by its crates.io version (https://crates.io/crates/roteiro/versions).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Roteiro, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Roteiro
abstract: >-
  A CLI that builds a provenance-tagged knowledge graph of a codebase — derived,
  authored and inferred facts kept distinct — and serves it to people and agents.
authors:
  - given-names: Mark
    family-names: Olliver
  - name: The Roteiro Project Team
repository-code: "https://github.com/OffeneDatenmodellierung/Roteiro"
url: "https://roteiro.dev"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - knowledge graph
  - provenance
  - code intelligence
  - architecture decision records
